Valid Submissions
Associates may claim up to INR 25,000 annually (or actuals); the reimbursed amount is taxable.
This reimbursement covers the associate and their dependents enrolled under the medical insurance policy.
For dependent claims, a copy of the Medical Insurance eCard must be attached.
Associates joining mid policy will be eligible for a prorated limit from their date of joining.
GST tax invoices from registered Indian vendors are preferred.
Invoices from non-GST vendors are acceptable if supported by proof of payment (e.g., UPI or card statement).
The invoice must be in the name of the associate or an enrolled dependent.
The invoice date must fall within the policy period and after the associates date of joining.
Multiple claims may be submitted in a year.
Claims must be submitted within 90 days from the invoice date.
If a subscription spans two financial years, the same invoice must be submitted separately for each financial year.
Purchases made within India or overseas are eligible.
For overseas purchases, the invoice must be in the associates or dependents name and include valid INR conversion proof (e.g., card/bank statement dated at purchase time).
Invalid Submissions
Handwritten receipt/invoice is not acceptable for Fitness Reimbursement.
Payment proof (UPI screenshot / Debit or Credit Card statement) not attached for Non-GST invoice.
Payment purpose not clearly mentioned on receipt
Currency conversion screenshot missing for international purchases.
Order summary or order confirmation is not accepted for Fitness Reimbursement.
Bills dated on or before 15 March 2026 are not eligible for the current financial year.
Associate name does not match payroll/payslip records.
MediAssist E-card of the dependent is mandatory for Fitness Reimbursement.
Bill amount prorated to current financial year.
Bill/Invoice missing vendor GST/VAT/TIN registration number.
Total bill amount does not match the amount claimed.
Submitted bills are not relevant to this reimbursement category.
Corrected/altered/overwritten bills are not accepted.
Claim form submitted without supporting invoice/documents.
Duplicate claim (already submitted in a previous month).
